1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:02,460
Now, hurry up and drop your weapon.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,180
Step back and get on your hands and knees.

3
00:00:08,340 --> 00:00:10,580
You move even one bit and I'll kill her.

4
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:14,900
Hey, Laios, she was one of Shuro's followers, wasn't she?

5
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:18,200
Oh, yeah, then she was tailing us this whole time.

6
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:21,100
You! Get the spell off me!

7
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:21,760
Huh?

8
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:25,000
The spell that's been cast on me! Hurry up and get rid of it!

9
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:27,980
Oh, um, do you know what kind it is?

10
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:29,820
Can't you tell just by looking?

11
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:32,000
I thought you knew black magic.

12
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:36,880
You gotta at least mention exactly where it was cast on you and what type it is.

13
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:40,900
It's actually not one type of spell but two.

14
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,740
The first one is here.

15
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:44,500
And the other...

16
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:47,940
Uh-uh.

17
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:50,240
...is my whole body.

18
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:54,520
Wait, does that mean she's a beast man?

19
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:57,520
Uh-huh. I saw one of these a long time ago.

20
00:00:57,520 --> 00:01:00,400
She's what's called an artificially made beast man.

21
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:04,400
I heard they're made using black magic to mix human and beast souls.

22
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:09,280
All right, then. I'll do whatever I can.

23
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:14,760
This text. Looks like it's written in the Eastern language.

24
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:16,580
What's the spell type?

25
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,540
Are you really a magic user?

26
00:01:19,020 --> 00:01:22,660
It's a curse that activates if the caster doesn't touch it within a set time.

27
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:25,300
So was the one who cast this that Miseru lady?

28
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:26,880
How long until it activates?

29
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:29,280
And what happens when the time is up?

30
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:30,000
Dunno.

31
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:32,020
So you might want to remove it quickly.

32
00:01:32,020 --> 00:01:34,840
I mean, you don't want to die with me, do you?

33
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:37,700
I'll let you go if you dispel it.

34
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:43,320
I'm not familiar with the letters, but I think I can remove this.

35
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:44,720
Hey, kid over there!

36
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:45,140
Huh?

37
00:01:45,380 --> 00:01:46,560
Bring me something to eat!

38
00:01:46,560 --> 00:02:00,200
Out of curiosity, when was the last time you ate?

39
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:03,680
If you eat like that without chewing, it'll get stuck in your throat.

40
00:02:04,060 --> 00:02:04,680
Shut up!

41
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:07,320
How about you let me fix you up a nice, warm meal?

42
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:08,680
Hey, didn't I say don't move?

43
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:11,060
Don't underestimate me!

44
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:16,940
All I'm gonna do is whip up something warm for your belly.

45
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:17,780
That's all.

46
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:21,720
If you try to make me eat monster parts, I'll kill you.

47
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:23,120
I understand.

48
00:02:24,620 --> 00:02:25,060
Hmm.

49
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:29,860
If I'm remembering right, we picked up some mushrooms near the dryads.

50
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:30,600
Hmm?

51
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:31,900
Hold on.

52
00:02:32,260 --> 00:02:33,700
Are those little feet it sprouted?

53
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:36,280
Probably my imagination.

54
00:02:37,780 --> 00:02:39,700
Place a pod inside the magic circle.

55
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:45,260
Toss some butter in to melt it, fry a few garlic cloves, and then add rice.

56
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:47,680
Add in mushrooms and season it.

57
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:51,000
Pour in water and let it simmer for a while.

58
00:02:55,880 --> 00:02:56,400
Hmm.

59
00:02:57,420 --> 00:03:02,360
It feels shameful to be making something this simple compared to the dishes I had been making.

60
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:07,280
But I hate the thought of letting a young'un go hungry, so I'll do whatever I've gotta do.

61
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:10,180
Well, at the very least, I could put some cheese in.

62
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:12,400
It's ready.

63
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:16,440
I'll leave it here.

64
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:18,280
Who'd even eat something like...

65
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:32,240
This kid.

66
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:34,760
She has no table manners.

67
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:36,020
None!

68
00:03:36,020 --> 00:03:38,520
Give me more, now!

69
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:42,200
Do you think etiquette in the East is different from how we learn it here?

70
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:42,880
Doubt it.

71
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:45,840
I've never once seen Shura eat as sloppy as she does.

72
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:48,320
She was probably just raised poorly.

73
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:50,180
Guess this is new for you.

74
00:03:50,180 --> 00:03:50,480
Huh?

75
00:03:50,480 --> 00:04:06,540
What did you do that for?

76
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:07,620
I hate mushrooms.

77
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:08,820
She's picky.

78
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:10,980
This has never happened before.

79
00:04:11,460 --> 00:04:11,980
Senshi.

80
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:15,300
Your spoon.

81
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:16,340
Huh?

82
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:19,080
You're not holding it in your hand the right way.

83
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:19,560
Hey!

84
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:21,920
Get any closer to me and you're dead meat!

85
00:04:22,140 --> 00:04:26,900
Take that spoon, hold it properly, and pick up every piece of food you dropped on the floor.

86
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:28,220
What the hell?

87
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:29,840
Hold on, me too!

88
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:31,980
You shouldn't move while I'm dispelling!

89
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:33,140
Ah!

90
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:39,060
Ah!

91
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:39,220
Ah!

92
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:39,740
Ah!

93
00:04:39,740 --> 00:04:40,000
Ah!

94
00:04:43,340 --> 00:04:43,900
Ah!

95
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:47,440
This is how you hold the spoon.

96
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,800
I can hold it how I want!

97
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:52,400
And this is the easiest way for me to do it!

98
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:53,460
I'm sure it is.

99
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:57,180
Being forced to hold something in a way you're not used to must be vexing.

100
00:04:57,660 --> 00:04:58,280
But still...

101
00:04:58,280 --> 00:04:59,560
Senshi, behind you!

102
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:00,060
Ah!

103
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:05,880
No effect.

104
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:08,020
Paper?

105
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:09,440
Senshi!

106
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:10,380
Be careful!

107
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:10,740
Ah!

108
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:15,680
It's called a Tsujihiki knife.

109
00:05:15,980 --> 00:05:18,640
It's a type of carving knife used to finely slice meat.

110
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:21,320
The length of the blade is long and sharp.

111
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:24,340
While it may look intimidating, it's actually delicate.

112
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:29,040
Now, what do you think would happen if you swung it while gripping it like that?

113
00:05:29,540 --> 00:05:30,000
Senshi!

114
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:45,720
As you can see, the tool's ability isn't used to its fullest, which can put you at a disadvantage.

115
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:54,520
Senshi!

116
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:55,740
Now, Laos!

117
00:05:55,740 --> 00:06:06,840
Catgirl, you're not hurt anywhere, are you?

118
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:10,660
I probably startled you, and I'm sorry about that.

119
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:15,940
But there are reasons why there's good and bad ways to hold even the simplest of tools.

120
00:06:16,640 --> 00:06:18,200
And I'd like you to keep that in mind.

121
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:21,720
Also keep in mind you can't move while having something dispelled.

122
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:24,700
If it were something worse, who knows what could have happened.

123
00:06:24,700 --> 00:06:28,960
Looks like your food already got cold.

124
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:30,840
Let me warm it up for you real quick.

125
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:34,180
All right.

126
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:36,640
So why were you even following us?

127
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:42,740
This curse on my body, I've been looking for a way to remove it for a really long time.

128
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:51,040
I eventually figured out that the curse is tied to black magic, but wasn't able to find a magic user who specialized in it.

129
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:54,160
Not until we ran into that long year, anyway.

130
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:55,140
Black...

131
00:06:55,140 --> 00:06:57,200
Ancient magic has several types.

132
00:06:57,300 --> 00:07:00,040
The one that I'm researching deals with drawing energy from a different...

133
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:00,720
No excuses!

134
00:07:01,240 --> 00:07:02,740
I know you're capable of it!

135
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:05,620
I've seen living proof of your work, after all.

136
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:08,860
You've combined a person and a monster with your black magic!

137
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:15,580
And you guys are going deeper into the dungeon so you can remove the curse on that woman, aren't you?

138
00:07:15,920 --> 00:07:18,920
In other words, that must mean you know of a way to get rid of it!

139
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:21,680
So then you should be able to break my curse too, right?

140
00:07:21,980 --> 00:07:25,320
Remove this beast soul that possessed me so I can finally be free!

141
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:31,940
I'm sorry, but that's just not something I can do for you.

142
00:07:32,820 --> 00:07:33,300
Huh?

143
00:07:34,220 --> 00:07:39,080
There are lots of things we still don't know about souls, but they're often compared to an egg.

144
00:07:40,340 --> 00:07:47,540
Usually, a soul is inside the body, or shell, but once the body breaks, the insides spill out and can't be put back together again.

145
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:52,980
A spell has been cast over this dungeon that creates a thick membrane on the inside of the shell.

146
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:56,200
So, even if the soul gets damaged, it won't leave.

147
00:07:56,980 --> 00:08:02,260
In your and Fallon's cases, at the moment, there are two souls inside a single shell.

148
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:07,940
Once two souls are mixed together, it's impossible to go back to how they were before.

149
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:12,240
I already knew all that, but to put it so bluntly is harsh.

150
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:19,460
Wait, what? Then, why are you guys still continuing on such a dangerous journey?

151
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:25,200
Well, for starters, I can't leave my sister in the state she's currently in.

152
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:30,040
She might kill the next adventurer she runs into, or they might kill her.

153
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:32,420
We have to do something before then.

154
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:37,500
Also, if we go back to the surface now, we'd get arrested for using black magic.

155
00:08:38,380 --> 00:08:41,160
Shiro probably will have reported this to the Island Lord.

156
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:46,720
So, you're saying I'm stuck like this forever?

157
00:08:47,220 --> 00:08:48,480
Hey, listen to me.

158
00:08:48,980 --> 00:08:52,640
This might be weird of me to say, but I'm really glad I ended up meeting you.

159
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:57,360
I have no idea what monster you're mixed with, but your speech and actions are perfectly human.

160
00:08:57,580 --> 00:08:59,380
Plus, you have no urge to murder anything.

161
00:08:59,380 --> 00:09:06,140
Looking at it a different way, if we manage to free Fallon, she could regain her original personality.

162
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:12,340
Just having learned that makes me feel, um, I'm really happy right now.

163
00:09:13,060 --> 00:09:13,540
Here.

164
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:13,920
Huh?

165
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:19,440
This might be different from what you expected it to be, but maybe try Sina in a positive light.

166
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:21,220
Think of it as a new opportunity.

167
00:09:21,220 --> 00:09:27,120
The Lord of the Dungeon is far superior to me when it comes to the handling of ancient magic.

168
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:32,160
If we try asking him, it's possible he'll teach us a thing or two about separating souls.

169
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:33,420
Hang on.

170
00:09:33,820 --> 00:09:35,780
Are you guys inviting me into your party?

171
00:09:36,380 --> 00:09:39,000
I mean, it'll be hard to return to the surface alone.

172
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:41,580
I think I heard before that your name's Asabi.

173
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:43,920
That was just an alias.

174
00:09:44,180 --> 00:09:45,340
Then what's your...

175
00:09:45,340 --> 00:09:45,920
Izutsumi.

176
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:48,020
My real name's Izutsumi.

177
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:49,480
And don't forget it.

178
00:09:51,220 --> 00:10:03,080
Laios, how long are you going to keep up this lifestyle?

179
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:04,520
Father?

180
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:06,940
You need to start living a proper life.

181
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:10,540
I didn't allow you to leave home just for you to become a dragon slayer.

182
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:12,500
Come back to the village.

183
00:10:13,020 --> 00:10:14,300
But Fallon is still...

184
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:15,820
You can forget about that girl.

185
00:10:15,820 --> 00:10:16,180
Huh?

186
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:20,380
Do you think someone like you could actually make it in the outside world?

187
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:23,940
You couldn't fit in at school or the army and ran away.

188
00:10:24,680 --> 00:10:27,460
You don't even have the skills to explore a dungeon either.

189
00:10:27,940 --> 00:10:32,620
Your party members are going to trick and rob you, just like the ones from your gold-stripping days.

190
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:35,220
Because you're horrible at judging people's character.

191
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:37,680
That was certainly true with me.

192
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:42,680
You had considered me to be a good friend, but I'd always been uncomfortable being around you.

193
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:43,900
You're so annoying!

194
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:45,220
We settled this already!

195
00:10:45,740 --> 00:10:47,740
Wait, come to think of it...

196
00:10:47,740 --> 00:10:49,440
Why are my parents even here?

197
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:51,680
I haven't seen them in over ten years.

198
00:10:52,340 --> 00:10:54,180
More importantly, where am I?

199
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:55,540
And what was I doing?

200
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:57,280
Let's see here.

201
00:10:57,280 --> 00:11:03,100
I was getting kind of worried about Marcille.

202
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:05,200
She'd been looking really tired.

203
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:10,100
Marcille, we'll take watch tonight, so you go get some rest.

204
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:11,040
Huh?

205
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:12,180
How come?

206
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:13,480
You don't have to do that.

207
00:11:13,620 --> 00:11:14,780
Don't worry about it.

208
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:15,420
It's fine.

209
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:16,520
What are you...

210
00:11:16,520 --> 00:11:18,420
What's going on?

211
00:11:19,020 --> 00:11:21,120
I'm not even tired enough to sleep yet.

212
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:21,820
All right?

213
00:11:21,880 --> 00:11:22,960
I'm getting up now.

214
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:29,580
Before long, her peaceful sleeping breaths turned into unsettling groans.

215
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:31,800
Marcille, what's wrong?

216
00:11:31,840 --> 00:11:32,380
Are you okay?

217
00:11:32,700 --> 00:11:34,160
This looks pretty serious.

218
00:11:34,420 --> 00:11:35,280
Is it a monster?

219
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:37,540
Yeah, a nightmare to be exact.

220
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:42,140
It possesses sleeping people, gives them bad dreams, and eats their emotions.

221
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:46,300
At this rate, Marcille will keep getting weaker and eventually die.

222
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:48,500
Rise and shine, Marcille!

223
00:11:48,580 --> 00:11:50,840
Don't force her awake or it'll damage her psyche.

224
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:56,300
When Shiro got possessed that one time, Fallon went inside his dream and saved them.

225
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:58,760
So, let's try out that method.

226
00:11:59,300 --> 00:11:59,960
Hang on.

227
00:12:00,060 --> 00:12:01,200
You're gonna go into her dream?

228
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:04,140
Someone has to make her realize that she can wake up from it.

229
00:12:04,580 --> 00:12:07,840
You simply use the one who's dreaming as a pillow and...

230
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:16,080
I remember now.

231
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:18,180
I was trying to save Marcille.

232
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:21,120
But this is my dream.

233
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:23,840
Looks like the nightmare got a little taste of me.

234
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:25,060
Well, that figures.

235
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:27,880
Man, they really know what people hate, don't they?

236
00:12:28,260 --> 00:12:31,600
Although, since I've realized this is a dream...

237
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:33,980
My strongest servant, I summon thee!

238
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:38,240
Huh.

239
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:41,900
Okay, now how do I go into Marcille's dream?

240
00:12:43,020 --> 00:12:45,780
She's right under my head at the moment, so...

241
00:12:45,780 --> 00:12:48,560
That should mean I can dig down to get to her.

242
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:54,100
This is why dreams are the best.

243
00:12:54,380 --> 00:12:55,860
Though it only works in your own.

244
00:12:55,860 --> 00:13:03,020
That was a close call.

245
00:13:03,340 --> 00:13:05,380
I almost woke up from the feeling of falling.

246
00:13:06,640 --> 00:13:07,420
Oh, wow.

247
00:13:08,140 --> 00:13:09,820
This is Marcille's dream, huh?

248
00:13:10,900 --> 00:13:12,280
It's pretty amazing.

249
00:13:12,940 --> 00:13:13,900
Is someone there?

250
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,960
What are you doing here?

251
00:13:16,520 --> 00:13:17,780
This place is dangerous.

252
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:18,840
You need to leave.

253
00:13:19,780 --> 00:13:21,360
Are you Marcille?

254
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:23,500
Who are you?

255
00:13:23,740 --> 00:13:24,920
It's me, Laios.

256
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:27,340
The two of us are currently inside your dream.

257
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:30,520
You should wake up so we can get out of this...

258
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:32,060
What's that?

259
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:34,140
Oh, no, it's coming.

260
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:35,800
I have to run.

261
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:37,200
What's coming?

262
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:38,580
Hurry up, this way!

263
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:41,080
It's swallowed them.

264
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:43,240
Papa and Pippi are gone now.

265
00:13:43,640 --> 00:13:44,680
Papa and Pippi?

266
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:47,400
A dream about being chased.

267
00:13:48,180 --> 00:13:50,200
It's a common dream, but still stressful.

268
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:52,580
What was it Fallon said?

269
00:13:53,300 --> 00:13:55,840
Nightmares really love to feed on emotional wounds.

270
00:13:56,580 --> 00:13:58,500
They evoke stressful memories or trauma

271
00:13:58,500 --> 00:14:00,740
and display them as bad dreams.

272
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:03,000
Then, they feed off the dreamer.

273
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:05,280
In order to prevent that,

274
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:06,820
you need to protect those wounds.

275
00:14:08,920 --> 00:14:11,980
However, it's risky, so don't try it, okay?

276
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:14,060
Alright, I got it.

277
00:14:14,460 --> 00:14:16,320
I'm gonna defeat that thing for you.

278
00:14:16,900 --> 00:14:17,920
You can't do that.

279
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:18,740
It's dangerous.

280
00:14:18,740 --> 00:14:20,700
No need to worry about me.

281
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,960
I'm a lot stronger than I...

282
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:36,200
What the hell is that thing?

283
00:14:36,340 --> 00:14:37,960
How am I supposed to know?

284
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:40,340
So that's Marcelle's fear?

285
00:14:41,340 --> 00:14:43,180
It seems a little over the top,

286
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:44,260
but even so,

287
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:46,080
I don't think that I'll be able to defeat it.

288
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:48,960
She knew that this was a dream,

289
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:50,620
that that thing wouldn't be a threat.

290
00:14:51,540 --> 00:14:52,940
I think we're safe now.

291
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:56,060
There's no such thing as safe here.

292
00:14:56,060 --> 00:14:58,560
No one can beat that monster.

293
00:15:00,020 --> 00:15:01,120
It'll be okay.

294
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:03,320
We're gonna figure out how to defeat it.

295
00:15:04,060 --> 00:15:07,280
What is this thing that Marcelle fears?

296
00:15:07,860 --> 00:15:09,100
It's definitely a monster.

297
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:12,080
It has slow, crawly-like movements,

298
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:13,120
several tentacles,

299
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:14,400
and a hearty appetite.

300
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:16,640
Not to mention it's gross.

301
00:15:17,460 --> 00:15:18,520
Maybe it's a bug?

302
00:15:18,520 --> 00:15:21,720
Hmm, there aren't many bugs that large, though.

303
00:15:22,300 --> 00:15:23,460
What kind could it be?

304
00:15:23,980 --> 00:15:24,640
What kind?

305
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:25,760
I know!

306
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:27,200
It's a worm!

307
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:29,720
Worms are a part of the dragon family.

308
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:31,380
Their atrophied eyes and legs

309
00:15:31,380 --> 00:15:32,520
make them caterpillar-like.

310
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:33,760
If they're hungry,

311
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:35,360
then they'll eat just about anything,

312
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:36,940
and they're weak to fire and light.

313
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:38,900
That's such a cool thing.

314
00:15:39,060 --> 00:15:39,960
Good job, me.

315
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:44,800
I didn't even hear it.

316
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:46,360
Watch out!

317
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:48,980
We gotta run!

318
00:15:49,980 --> 00:15:52,440
That thing didn't touch you just now, did it?

319
00:15:52,740 --> 00:15:54,180
It was only a scratch.

320
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:54,820
Show me!

321
00:15:57,900 --> 00:15:59,600
What is this?

322
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:09,760
Crap.

323
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:11,380
She's even more scared.

324
00:16:11,920 --> 00:16:13,440
The nightmare's starting to get stronger.

325
00:16:18,180 --> 00:16:19,780
What vicious poison.

326
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:22,880
What happens if I die in someone else's dream?

327
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:24,160
No.

328
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:26,620
I'll fall right into its trap if I get anxious.

329
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,480
I've got to cheer her up.

330
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:30,100
It'll be okay.

331
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:32,100
You've got magic on your side.

332
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:34,320
Defeating something like that'll be no problem.

333
00:16:36,140 --> 00:16:36,700
Magic.

334
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:44,120
This place became even more unstable.

335
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:46,000
Did I say something bad?

336
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,120
I already...

337
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:51,100
I already tried using some of my magic to defeat the monster,

338
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:54,380
and that's how she ended up looking like this.

339
00:16:55,520 --> 00:16:56,120
She?

340
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:57,500
Wait a minute.

341
00:16:57,700 --> 00:16:58,940
Is that doll Fallon?

342
00:16:58,940 --> 00:17:00,620
I get it now.

343
00:17:01,300 --> 00:17:04,340
Marcelle feels guilty about what her magic turned Fallon into.

344
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:06,760
Then defeating the monster must mean...

345
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:09,920
The thing Marcelle fears is death!

346
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:12,400
It's here again!

347
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:15,160
You can't just run away all the time.

348
00:17:15,480 --> 00:17:17,300
You need to stand your ground and fight!

349
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:19,320
Don't worry.

350
00:17:19,540 --> 00:17:21,400
There's nothing to be afraid of, Marcelle.

351
00:17:22,340 --> 00:17:24,880
If you die in this dungeon, you can get revived.

352
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:25,740
Like Fallon.

353
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:28,360
She's alive because you used revival magic on her.

354
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:30,840
Besides, you're used to seeing corpses, right?

355
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:37,880
Oh, no!

356
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:38,860
It's sucking me in!

357
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:42,240
Wait, why is it only trying to pull me in?

358
00:17:42,340 --> 00:17:43,440
Grab my hand!

359
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:48,200
It's not poison.

360
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:50,780
I'm aging at an incredibly fast rate.

361
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:53,860
Hey, hold on a second, Marcelle.

362
00:17:54,140 --> 00:17:55,440
I can't breathe.

363
00:17:56,060 --> 00:17:57,140
Something's weird here.

364
00:17:57,700 --> 00:17:59,720
Is there a living creature that can do this?

365
00:18:00,400 --> 00:18:01,940
Maybe it's not a living thing at all.

366
00:18:02,700 --> 00:18:05,120
Does this mean you're gonna end up leaving me too?

367
00:18:05,620 --> 00:18:06,120
No.

368
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:08,400
I'll be able to run again after I rest.

369
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:09,120
Liar!

370
00:18:09,700 --> 00:18:11,640
Everybody gives up on running with me!

371
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:13,360
Then that thing swallows them!

372
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:17,300
Papa, Pippi, Fallon, and everyone else too!

373
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:20,140
That's why I worked so hard to study lots of magic!

374
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:24,020
But if learning and using that magic made Fallon go away,

375
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:26,460
then what was it all for?

376
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:30,780
If I could maybe ask, did your father die at a young age?

377
00:18:31,180 --> 00:18:34,080
We were at Papa's funeral, and Mama said

378
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:38,040
that when I run, I go a lot faster than everyone else.

379
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:42,600
So that means I'm gonna have to say goodbye to a whole bunch of people.

380
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:44,460
You keep mentioning Pippi.

381
00:18:44,860 --> 00:18:45,600
Who is that?

382
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:46,300
My bird.

383
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:47,860
I see.

384
00:18:48,700 --> 00:18:51,280
So it's not that Marcelle is afraid of death.

385
00:18:51,780 --> 00:18:55,100
She's actually worried her loved ones will die before she does.

386
00:18:55,100 --> 00:19:03,180
You need to calm down, Marcelle.

387
00:19:03,360 --> 00:19:05,900
The more scared you become, the stronger it gets.

388
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:07,720
What am I supposed to do?

389
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:08,840
I can't fight it!

390
00:19:08,940 --> 00:19:09,900
I can't do anything!

391
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:11,340
No, you can!

392
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:13,700
Because you're Marcelle, and you're amazing!

393
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:16,260
I mean, these books say it all.

394
00:19:16,940 --> 00:19:19,380
I didn't see anything like this while in my dream.

395
00:19:20,040 --> 00:19:22,260
You've been working hard for a long time, right?

396
00:19:22,660 --> 00:19:23,500
Don't get discouraged!

397
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:25,080
Have confidence in yourself!

398
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:27,120
Marcelle, stay strong!

399
00:19:27,460 --> 00:19:27,860
No!

400
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:29,080
That's enough!

401
00:19:29,080 --> 00:19:30,300
Let's just run!

402
00:19:30,420 --> 00:19:31,500
Please, stand up!

403
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:34,320
How can I be strong when my magic's incomplete?

404
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:40,460
If only I had that book you was carrying with him, I'd finally be able to complete my magic!

405
00:19:40,660 --> 00:19:42,240
Then go ahead and wish for that!

406
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:45,480
If you wish hard enough for it, you can do anything!

407
00:19:45,700 --> 00:19:46,800
So don't be afraid!

408
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,880
You'll do it better the next time you try!

409
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:50,380
Don't give up, Marcelle!

410
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:51,580
Don't go!

411
00:19:51,740 --> 00:19:52,380
You can't!

412
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:53,420
Please, no!

413
00:19:53,420 --> 00:19:54,020
No!

414
00:20:03,620 --> 00:20:04,220
Yeah!

415
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:05,240
That's the spirit!

416
00:20:05,580 --> 00:20:05,880
Go!

417
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:17,680
Wait a minute.

418
00:20:17,860 --> 00:20:20,000
Is that even how you're supposed to use that?

419
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:25,100
Oh, you're finally awake.

420
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:27,300
You were both groaning in your sleep.

421
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:28,120
Are you okay?

422
00:20:28,580 --> 00:20:30,440
I really don't remember what happened.

423
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:33,620
I think I dreamt about being tired or something.

424
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:39,280
Just going back to sleep!

425
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:40,160
No, please!

426
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:41,240
You have to stay awake!

427
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:43,460
My dream?

428
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:48,360
I can't remember it, but from what I can tell, it was probably a fun one.

429
00:20:48,360 --> 00:20:50,100
Looks like my plan actually worked.

430
00:20:50,280 --> 00:20:51,320
Did something happen?

431
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:53,120
Pass your pillow to me.

432
00:20:53,640 --> 00:20:54,020
Hmm?

433
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:58,240
What's that?

434
00:20:58,420 --> 00:20:59,500
This thing is a nightmare.

435
00:21:00,220 --> 00:21:03,600
It sneaks inside of people's pillows and gives them bad dreams.

436
00:21:04,260 --> 00:21:05,860
But there sure are a lot of them.

437
00:21:06,600 --> 00:21:08,560
They must have been hiding in your pillow for a while.

438
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:09,520
Seriously?

439
00:21:10,020 --> 00:21:11,600
Senshi, do you think we can eat these?

440
00:21:11,820 --> 00:21:13,780
I've been curious about what they taste like.

441
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:14,960
Yeah, of course we can.

442
00:21:14,960 --> 00:21:17,880
First, make it spit out any dirt.

443
00:21:19,340 --> 00:21:21,720
By soaking them in some hot water like this.

444
00:21:22,580 --> 00:21:22,820
Huh?

445
00:21:23,340 --> 00:21:25,800
Another name that the nightmare goes by is Shen.

446
00:21:26,080 --> 00:21:27,660
It's part of the dragon family.

447
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:30,020
They kind of look like dragons, don't you think?

448
00:21:30,100 --> 00:21:31,240
You're joking, right?

449
00:21:31,660 --> 00:21:36,180
After melting some butter, place the nightmares in the pan and pour a bit of wine over top.

450
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:37,300
Then cover.

451
00:21:37,300 --> 00:21:43,960
To finish the dish, add a touch of soy sauce.

452
00:21:44,620 --> 00:21:45,740
And it's ready.

453
00:21:48,220 --> 00:21:49,060
What's this?

454
00:21:50,060 --> 00:21:51,560
That's me when I was little.

455
00:21:51,820 --> 00:21:54,580
The dream that the nightmares ate turned into a mirage.

456
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:57,520
I think I'm starting to remember things.

457
00:21:57,780 --> 00:21:58,600
Yeah, that's right.

458
00:21:58,800 --> 00:22:02,200
I was running away from something and suddenly a fluffy dog appeared.

459
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:06,520
The dog and I went on an adventure to search for treasure together.

460
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:09,260
It was a really fun dream.

461
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:11,060
That's a pretty dirty looking dog.

462
00:22:11,280 --> 00:22:12,720
It doesn't look all that smart.

463
00:22:13,260 --> 00:22:14,400
What's wrong, Laios?

464
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:18,240
The way I remember it, it was a silver wolf and not a dog.

465
00:22:18,960 --> 00:22:19,340
Oh well.

466
00:22:19,920 --> 00:22:23,140
If I was able to help make her dream fun, then I'm glad.

467
00:22:23,140 --> 00:22:28,100
Oh, yeah.

468
00:22:32,500 --> 00:22:34,400
Oh, yeah.

469
00:22:34,400 --> 00:22:35,020
Oh, yeah.

470
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:35,820
Yeah.

471
00:22:35,840 --> 00:22:47,880
Oh, yeah.

472
00:22:47,880 --> 00:22:48,220
Oh, yeah.

473
00:22:48,220 --> 00:22:52,280
Oh, yeah.

474
00:22:52,340 --> 00:22:52,660
Oh, yeah.

